name: sim.insertVoxelsIntoOctree
description: Inserts voxels into an OC tree. Each voxel will store a color and a tag value
luaSynopsis: int totalVoxelCnt = sim.insertVoxelsIntoOctree(int octreeHandle, int options, list points, list color = None, list tag = None)
pythonSynopsis: int totalVoxelCnt = sim.insertVoxelsIntoOctree(int octreeHandle, int options, float[] points, int[] color = nil, int[] tag = nil)
inputs:
1. octreeHandle: handle of the OC tree, can be combined with sim.handleflag_codedstring, when one wishes to provide point data as a float buffer, color data as a char buffer and tag as an uint32 buffer
2. options: bit-coded:
    - bit0 set (1): specified points are relative to the OC tree reference frame, otherwise they are relative to the world reference frame
    - bit1 set (2): the color array contains one RGB triple per point, and the tag array contains one value per point. Otherwise it the color array contains a single RGB triple, and the tag array contains a single value.
3. points: array of voxel positions specified as x/y/z coordinates
4. color: array of one or several RGB triplets, specifying the red, green and blue color components (0-255). Can be None/nil
5. tag: array of one or several uint32 values, which are user-defined values. Can be None/nil
outputs:
1. totalVoxelCnt: the total number of voxels in the OC tree
replacedBy:
- name: addVoxels, class: ocTree, file: ocTree_addVoxels.method
- name: addPackedVoxels, class: ocTree, file: ocTree_addPackedVoxels.method
